          "en": "Article 16\nIf there is a clerical error, miscalculation or mistake in a tax assessment letter such as a typing error, an error in the amount, an error in the application of the rate, the Director General of Taxes ex officio or at the request of the Taxpayer may correct the erroneous or mistaken Tax Assessment Letter/Additional Tax Assessment Letter.\nThe meaning of correcting in this paragraph may be adding, reducing or eliminating, depending on the nature of the error or mistake."
