          "en": "Article 17\nParagraph (1) letter a.\nA Tax Overpayment Refund Decision Letter (SKKPP) may be issued after the Director General of Taxes has conducted a study or audit with the intention of ascertaining and giving assurance that there is truly an overpayment of the amount of tax owed.\nThe said Tax Overpayment Refund Decision Letter must be issued within a maximum period of twelve months after the application letter is received. With such a time limit, apart from taking into account the interest of legal certainty for the Taxpayer, it is also intended for the interest of orderly tax administration.\nParagraph (1) letter b.\nA Notification Letter may be issued after the Director General of Taxes has conducted a study or audit with the intention of ascertaining and giving assurance that the amount of tax paid by the Taxpayer and withheld/collected by a third party is truly equal to the amount of tax owed.\nParagraph (2)\nSufficiently clear."
