          "en": "Article 8\n(1) The income or loss of a woman who is married at the beginning of the tax year, as well as losses from previous years that have not been compensated as referred to in Article 6 paragraph (3), are deemed to be the income or loss of her husband, except the wife's income from work that has been withheld for tax based on Article 21 and that has no connection with the business of the husband or other family members.\n(2) The income of a minor child not derived from work, and income from work connected with the business of other family members, shall be combined with the income of his or her parents.\nArticle 9 …"
