          "en": "Article 16\nTaxable income is the calculation basis for determining the amount of Income Tax payable.\nAs stated in Article 2 paragraph (2), there are 2 (two) groups of taxpayers recognised, namely:\ndomestic taxpayers and\nforeign taxpayers.\nFor domestic taxpayers, basically there are 2 (two) methods to determine the amount of taxable income:\n- method …\n- the ordinary calculation method,\n- the calculation method using the Computation Norm.\nParagraph (1)\nThe ordinary calculation method\nExample:\n- Income obtained in a tax year according to Article 4 paragraph (1) Rp50,000,000\n- Costs according to Article 6 paragraph (1):\ncosts to obtain, collect and maintain income\nRp30,000,000\ndepreciation and amortisation Rp6,000,000\ncontributions to pension fund Rp1,000,000\nRp37,000,000\n- Net income..............Rp13,000,000\n- Compensation of losses of previous years\nRp2,000,000\n- Taxable income (for corporate entities, other than cooperative entities)........Rp11,000,000\n- For cooperative entities it is permitted to deduct the refund of the residual business surplus obtained from activities from and for members\n- Deduction for individual taxpayers Article 7 paragraph (1), for example a taxpayer married with 2 (two) dependent children...............Rp2,400,000\n- Taxable income..........Rp8,600,000\nParagraph (2)\nThe use of the Computation Norm is applied to certain taxpayers, namely taxpayers whose business turnover or gross receipts from independent work in a year amount to less than Rp60,000,000 (sixty million rupiah).\nFor taxpayers whose business turnover or gross receipts from independent work in a year amount to less than Rp60,000,000 (sixty million rupiah), according to the provisions of this Law they are not required to keep books. For them the calculation of taxable income is carried out using the Computation Norm.\nHowever, …\nHowever, if desired by the taxpayer, the calculation of taxable income may be carried out by the ordinary calculation method as referred to in paragraph (1), provided that they keep books as regulated in this Law.\n(See the elucidation on Article 14).\nParagraph (3)\nSufficiently clear."
