          "en": "Article 20\nParagraph (1)\nSettlement of tax in the current year, so that at year-end it approaches the amount of tax payable, is carried out through:\na. withholding …\na. withholding and collection of tax by other parties where income is obtained by the taxpayer from work (work in an employment relationship and independent work) as referred to in Article 21, collection of tax on income from business as referred to in Article 22, and withholding of tax on income from capital and certain services as referred to in Article 23.\nb. in addition to settlement of tax through withholding or collection of tax by other parties, the taxpayer itself shall also make payments in the current year as referred to in Article 25.\nParagraph (2)\nSettlement of tax in the current year constitutes instalments of tax payments which may later be taken into account by crediting them against the Income Tax payable for the entire tax year concerned.\nParagraph (3)\nSufficiently clear.\nParagraph (4)\nSufficiently clear."
